.Sh HISTORY
These functions combine timely's
.Vt Config
types, and their command-line options, as of timely-dataflow 0.31.
Upstream parses with the getopts crate and fails on options it does
not recognize.
.Fn dtfl_config_from_args
uses no global state and keeps unrecognized options for the caller.
Upstream accepts
.Fl n
or
.Fl w
of 0, and a
.Fl p
outside the cluster, and fails later.
This parser rejects them.
.Fn dtfl_config_set_spill_file
is timely's
.Vt Hooks::spill
with the file-backed
.Vt Threshold
and
.Vt PrefetchPolicy
pair from its
.Pa spill_compare
example.
Upstream takes any policy factory and reads a spilled file back whole
on the first fetch; libdtfl offers only the file strategy and reads
back one buffer at a time.
Timely 0.13 removed
.Ev TIMELY_WORKER_LOG_ADDR ;
libdtfl restores it, but reads it only through the caller's
.Fa lookup .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A configuration may be read from several threads at once, but must not
be modified while another thread uses it.
.Fn dtfl_config_from_args
and
.Fn dtfl_config_from_env
touch no global state.
